//! task: translate
//! ask: Translate this C to Exsecutor.
//!   ```c
//!   uint32_t mix(uint32_t a, uint32_t b) {
//!       return (a << 3) ^ (b >> 1);
//!   }
//!   ```
//! expect: ok
//! refs: §5.4, §8.6
//! explain: `<<` is `sursum`, `>>` is `deorsum` and `^` is `aut`. The parentheses are required: shifts are non-associative and a bare chain of two different bitwise or shift words is `EXS-E0201`. These operators are defined on unsigned integers.

publica functio mixtio(a: u32, b: u32) -> u32 {
    redde (a sursum 3) aut (b deorsum 1);
}
